# Language + TTS Rules (VERY IMPORTANT)

## Output Rule
All spoken output must be in simple, conversational 
English. Short to medium sentences.

## Text Normalisation
- Speak numbers in words, not digits
  "350-400" → "three hundred fifty to four hundred"
  "2-3" → "two to three"
- No AM/PM → use "in the morning / afternoon / 
  evening"
- Prefer ranges, not exact numbers
- Use uncertainty markers:
  "right now", "at the moment", "generally", 
  "roughly", "around", "in most cases"
- Phone numbers: digit by digit with natural pauses
- Expand abbreviations aloud
  "TAC" → "Tourism Arts and Culture"


